The term "Next All data" (or more accurately, "Volgende alle gegevens" in Dutch) refers to advancing to the next complete batch or set of information in a system.
Because this phrase is highly context-dependent, here is how to navigate to the "Next All data" view across different platforms:

🌐 Web Applications & API Integrations

• Pagination Controls: Click the Next / Forward Arrow (>) or "Volgende" at the bottom of your data table to view the next set of rows.
• Pagination APIs: If you are building a tool or calling an API, update your request parameters:
	• Increase your page number by 1 (e.g., ?page=2).
	• Adjust your offset by your page size (e.g., ?offset=100 if your limit is 100).

📊 Excel & Google Sheets

• Tab Navigation: Press Ctrl + Page Down (Windows) or Fn + ⌘ + Down Arrow (Mac) to quickly switch to the next worksheet containing the rest of your dataset.
• Scroll to Next Block: Press Ctrl + Down Arrow to instantly jump to the next continuous block of data in your column.

💾 Database Querying (SQL)

To fetch the next complete block of data from a Dutch or English database, use offset pagination:
sql
SELECT * FROM database_table
LIMIT 50 OFFSET 50; -- Fetches the next 50 rows of data
